# Field-Oriented Control (FOC) of BLDC Motor

## Overview

This project focuses on the design and simulation of a **sensored Field-Oriented Control (FOC) system for a three-phase BLDC/PMSM motor using MATLAB/Simulink**.

The system is designed to achieve precise **torque, speed, and position control** using a cascaded control architecture consisting of PI controllers, Clarke and Park transformations, Inverse Park Transformation, Space Vector PWM (SVPWM), a three-phase inverter, and rotor position feedback.

## Objectives

- Develop a complete FOC-based BLDC/PMSM motor drive in MATLAB/Simulink.
- Implement closed-loop **torque control**.
- Implement closed-loop **speed control**.
- Implement closed-loop **position control**.
- Regulate the motor's d-axis and q-axis currents independently.
- Generate inverter switching signals using SVPWM.
- Incorporate rotor position and speed feedback.
- Evaluate the motor response under different reference commands and load disturbances.

## Control Architecture

The overall control structure follows a cascaded approach:

```text
Position Reference (θ*)
        │
        ▼
 Position PI Controller
        │
        ▼
 Speed Reference (ω*)
        │
        ▼
   Speed PI Controller
        │
        ▼
 q-axis Current Reference (Iq*)
        │
        ├───────────────┐
        │               │
       Iq*             Id* = 0
        │               │
        ▼               ▼
     PI (q)           PI (d)
        │               │
       Vq*             Vd*
        └───────┬───────┘
                │
                ▼
       Inverse Park Transform
                │
                ▼
             Vα, Vβ
                │
                ▼
              SVPWM
                │
                ▼
          PWM Gate Signals
                │
                ▼
       Three-Phase Inverter
                │
                ▼
           BLDC/PMSM Motor
                │
        ┌───────┴────────┐
        │                │
     Ia, Ib, Ic       Rotor Position
        │                │
        ▼                ▼
     Clarke           Encoder/
   Transform          QEP Feedback
        │                │
        ▼                ▼
     Iα, Iβ             θe
        │
        ▼
      Park
    Transform
        │
        ▼
      Id, Iq
        │
        └──── Feedback
